@startuml
title M-SH4 - SH1 gate deployment, provenance and cutover (not SH2 activation)
left to right direction

cloud "Private board repository\nowner: board" as private_repo {
  artifact "Pinned source commit\nunchanged tests / fixtures / goldens" as source
  artifact "Private full consumer workflow" as private_workflow
}
cloud "Public swarma-session-host repository\nowner: module" as public_repo {
  artifact "Candidate production snapshot\npublic immutable module tag at Z/C1" as candidate
  artifact "Generic gate tooling / invented fixture\ncurrent prototype; no package moved" as tooling
}
artifact "Shared evidence tuple (§2.4-2.5 / What F records)\nboard commit / host tree / candidate manifest and module graph\ngenerator / transform / helper / adapters / tests / fixtures / goldens\ncommands + real exit codes / inventories / mutation named tests\ntoolchain / environment / runner class / workflow identity" as tuple

node "Lane 1 - public module CI\nGitHub-hosted macOS and Ubuntu\nprocesses: checkout helper, projector, Go test / mutation runners" as lane1 {
  artifact "Disposable private pinned board checkout\ncandidate production at original import path\ntest bytes / fixtures / goldens unchanged and hashed" as projection
  artifact "Inventory / guard reached:expected / mutation evidence\ncurrent prototype: macOS gating, Ubuntu informative" as lane1_reports
}
node "Lane 2 - private board release CI\nGitHub-hosted Ubuntu\nprocesses: board build / full CI / converter and CLI exercises" as lane2 {
  artifact "Real board consumer\nimmutable public module tag\nno candidate replacement" as consumer
  artifact "Whole board CI evidence\nconfiguration / board / vendor drift / build / docs guards\nall CLI packages / server / regressions" as lane2_reports
}
node "Lane 3 - public module CI\nGitHub-hosted macOS and Ubuntu\nprocesses: vet / race tests / build / conformance runners" as lane3 {
  artifact "Module vet / race / build\ndeclared macOS and Linux conformance (after extraction)" as module_checks
  artifact "Current generic tooling checks\nprove tooling only, not extraction or module conformance" as tooling_checks
}
node "Current public lane 2 prototype\nGitHub-hosted Ubuntu\nprocesses: consumer helper / Go build and vet" as prototype {
  artifact "Candidate via file GOPROXY\nboard build/vet only; not full release gate" as proxy
}
artifact "Allowlisted run reports\nowner: CI run / attached Change Request\nno private checkout, raw logs or proxy archive in artifacts" as reports
component "Operator-controlled C1 maintenance transaction\nboard tb-sessiond executable retained through C1\npaired board build + public module serving library" as cutover

source --> projection : public CI private pinned checkout\naccepted board-code exposure in public logs (2026-10-10)
candidate --> projection : production projection only / deterministic declared adapters
projection --> lane1_reports : discovered / executed / skipped / tagged inventories\nguard target ratios and named-test mutations
private_workflow --> consumer : release workflow owner
candidate --> consumer : immutable tag; whole private consumer CI
consumer --> lane2_reports
candidate --> module_checks : extracted module proof still future
tooling --> tooling_checks : public tooling / invented fixture
candidate --> proxy : current prototype path
tuple ..> lane1_reports : same candidate/source binding
tuple ..> lane2_reports : immutable release identity at Z/C1
tuple ..> module_checks : same released candidate
lane1_reports --> reports
lane2_reports --> reports
module_checks --> reports
tooling_checks --> reports
proxy --> reports : bounded prototype evidence
reports --> cutover : release evidence + operator maintenance, not automatic deployment

note bottom of lane1
  Corrected spec §2.4 supersedes audit B4's old private-projection layout.
  Private checkout and public logs are distinct from artifact publication.
  Raw private bytes are never uploaded as lane artifacts.
  Opt-in smoke / tagged mutation status remains explicit, never hidden.
end note
note bottom of tuple
  No invented tuple wire format, artifact retention or CI process UIDs:
  unspecified in spec §2.4 / docs gate guide.
  The earlier F failure rule is replaced; proof runs on all three lanes at Z/C1.
  Cut-first work stays in a private working fork.
  Board repository keeps its in-tree session package/dependencies until C1.
  Z proof failure: no immutable tag; fork stays on the commit-pinned module.
  Board repository unchanged; fix module/fork and rerun Z.
  C1 proof failure: defer cutover (§2.6); quiescence/rollback unchanged.
  Tests/builds run on CI, never development host.
end note
note bottom of cutover
  Not before conference window ends (19 October).
  Refuse/defer if all start paths cannot be quiesced or one writer unproven.
  Hold exclusive state ownership through snapshot / swap / start / health check.
  Paired manifest binds board build, module tag, wire/goal/storage schemas
  and permitted reader/writer pairs; replacement guard remains.
  Reopen only with paired identity and verified single writer.
  Rollback requires old reader accepts every retained schema;
  never erase later records by restoring an old snapshot (§2.6).
end note
note bottom of reports
  Suites and tooling do not establish SH2 canons or runtime migration.
  Relevant runtime ownership at SH1: board-composed tb-sessiond owns
  Claude PTY / private per-session Codex app-server (§1 / §2.2).
end note

